---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site stores and sends.">
  <div class="page-head"><h1>Privacy</h1></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>There are no accounts, no logins and no tracking cookies.</p>
    <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Progress</strong> (which lessons you marked complete), your <strong>theme</strong>, your <strong>lab graphs</strong> and your <strong>code lab code</strong> are saved in your browser's localStorage. They never leave your device. Clear your site data to remove them. To move them to another device, use <a href={href('/progress/')}>Your progress</a>: it downloads a file to your device and imports it on the other one, without uploading anything.</li>
      <li>If you paste an <strong>API key</strong> into a code lab, it is kept in sessionStorage for that tab only and sent directly from your browser to the model provider. It is never sent to this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What is loaded from elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Code labs download Python (Pyodide) from cdn.jsdelivr.net the first time you press Run.</li>
      <li>If the site owner enables Vercel or Cloudflare Web Analytics, it counts page views without cookies or personal data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
